Subject: [PATCH] builtin.conf: the libmpv profile leaves the builtin scripts unloaded

mpv_create() applies the [libmpv] profile, which turns the OSC off and
nothing else of the builtin scripts: stats, console, auto_profiles,
select, positioning, commands and context_menu still load in every
player an embedder creates. Each is a Lua state on a thread of its own,
mpv_initialize() starts them all, and the first loadfile waits until
every one has run its top level. None of them can be reached in an
Android app: the same profile removes the default key bindings and the
terminal, and there is no config file for auto_profiles to read a
profile from.

The profile now sets their options to no. It is applied before the
embedder sets anything, so an option set to yes afterwards, before or
after mpv_initialize(), loads that script as before (with
load-stats-overlay and load-console set back, exactly lua/stats and
lua/console run). ytdl is left as it was.

Unpatched against patched library with the options Plezy sets (it sets
none of these), interleaved, from the player's creation to the first
frame of a local H.264 MP4, median (range):
  SEI Box R 4K Plus, n = 5       534 (516-562) -> 457 (435-489) ms
  Fire TV Stick 4K 2nd gen, n = 10
                                 391 (344-424) -> 339 (269-393) ms
  Pixel 7, n = 5                 144 (132-147) -> 123 (120-144) ms
Process CPU up to that frame 740 -> 680, 670 -> 565 and 280 -> 230 ms;
six threads fewer for as long as the player lives, and 3.6 MB less
native heap in an idle player on both boxes.

--- a/etc/builtin.conf
+++ b/etc/builtin.conf
@@ -24,6 +24,18 @@ idle=yes
 terminal=no
 input-terminal=no
 osc=no
+# Android: the other builtin scripts stay unloaded too. Each one is a Lua state
+# on a thread of its own in every player, the first loadfile waits until all of
+# them have run their top level, and none can be reached here: there are no
+# default key bindings (below), no terminal, and auto_profiles has no config
+# file to read a profile from. An embedder that wants one sets its option back.
+load-stats-overlay=no
+load-console=no
+load-auto-profiles=no
+load-select=no
+load-positioning=no
+load-commands=no
+load-context-menu=no
 input-default-bindings=no
 input-vo-keyboard=no
 # macOS global input hooks
